    "D": "-5\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (D)\nAns. (D)\nSol. $f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{cc}\\frac{\\ln (1+5 x)-\\ln (1+\\alpha x)}{x} & ; x \\neq 0 \\\\ 10 & ; x=0\\end{array}\\right.$\n$$\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\ln (1+5 x)-\\ln (1+\\alpha x)}{x}=10$$\n\nUsing expension\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\n\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{(5 x+\\ldots . .)-(\\alpha x+\\ldots \\ldots)}{x}=10 \\\\\n5-\\alpha=10 \\Rightarrow \\alpha=-5\n\\end{array}$$\n5. If [t] denotes the greatest integer $\\leq \\mathrm{t}$, then the value of $\\int_{0}^{1}\\left[2 \\mathrm{x}-\\left|3 \\mathrm{x}^{2}-5 \\mathrm{x}+2\\right|+1\\right] \\mathrm{dx}$ is:\n(A) $\\frac{\\sqrt{37}+\\sqrt{13}-4}{6}$\n(B) $\\frac{\\sqrt{37}-\\sqrt{13}-4}{6}$\n(C) $\\frac{-\\sqrt{37}-\\sqrt{13}+4}{6}$\n(D) $\\frac{-\\sqrt{37}+\\sqrt{13}+4}{6}$\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (A)\nAns. (A)\nSol. $\\mathrm{I}=\\int_{0}^{\\mathrm{l}}\\left[2 \\mathrm{x}-13 \\mathrm{x}^{2}-3 \\mathrm{x}-2 \\mathrm{x}+21+1\\right] \\mathrm{dx}$\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\nI=\\int_{0}^{1}[2 x-|(3 x-2)(x-1)|] d x+\\int_{0}^{1} 1 d x \\\\\nI=\\int_{0}^{2 / 3}\\left[\\left(2 x-\\left(3 x^{2}-5 x+2\\right)\\right)\\right] d x+\\int_{2 / 3}^{1}\\left(2 x+\\left(3 x^{2}-5 x+2\\right)\\right) d x+1 \\\\\nI=\\int_{0}^{2 / 3}\\left[-3 x^{2}+7 x-2\\right] d x+\\int_{2 / 3}^{1}\\left(3 x^{2}-3 x+2\\right) d x+1\n\\end{array}$$\n$$y=-3 x^{2}+7 x-2$$\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\n\\int_{0}^{\\alpha}(-2) \\mathrm{dx}+\\int_{\\alpha}^{1 / 3}(-1) \\mathrm{dx}+\\int_{1 / 3}^{\\beta} 0 \\mathrm{dx}+\\int_{\\beta}^{2 / 3} 1 . \\mathrm{dx} \\\\\n=-2 \\alpha-\\left(\\frac{1}{3}-\\alpha\\right)+\\frac{2}{3}-\\beta=-\\alpha-\\beta+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\\n\\mathrm{y}=3 \\mathrm{x}^{2}-3 \\mathrm{x}+2\n\\end{array}$$\n\nWhen $\\mathrm{x} \\in\\left(\\frac{2}{3}, 1\\right)$\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\n3 x^{2}-3 x+2 \\in\\left(\\frac{4}{3}, 2\\right) \\\\\n{\\left[3 x^{2}-3 x+2\\right]=1} \\\\\n\\therefore \\int_{2 / 3}^{1}\\left[3 x^{2}-3 x+2\\right] d x=1\\left(1-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)=\\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{array}$$\n\nHence $\\mathrm{I}=\\left(\\frac{1}{3}-(\\alpha+\\beta)\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)+1$\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\n=\\frac{5}{3}-\\left(\\frac{7-\\sqrt{37}}{6}+\\frac{7-\\sqrt{13}}{6}\\right) \\\\\n=\\frac{-2}{3}+\\frac{\\sqrt{37}+\\sqrt{13}}{6} \\\\\n=\\frac{\\sqrt{37}+\\sqrt{13}-4}{6}\n\\end{array}$$\n\nJEE Exam Solution\nwww.esaral.com\n2"
